        "solution": "#### Step 1: Calculate the Axis Intercepts for Both Constraint Lines\n1. **Line $D_1 : 3x_1 + 4x_2 = 12$**\n   - If $x_1 = 0 \\implies 4x_2 = 12 \\implies x_2 = 3 \\implies$ Point $(0, 3)$\n   - If $x_2 = 0 \\implies 3x_1 = 12 \\implies x_1 = 4 \\implies$ Point $(4, 0)$\n   - Test $(0,0)$: $0 \\le 12$ (True ✅ $\\rightarrow$ region is below $D_1$).\n\n2. **Line $D_2 : 7x_1 + 2x_2 = 14$**\n   - If $x_1 = 0 \\implies 2x_2 = 14 \\implies x_2 = 7 \\implies$ Point $(0, 7)$\n   - If $x_2 = 0 \\implies 7x_1 = 14 \\implies x_1 = 2 \\implies$ Point $(2, 0)$\n   - Test $(0,0)$: $0 \\le 14$ (True ✅ $\\rightarrow$ region is below $D_2$).\n\n---\n\n#### Step 2: Identify the Feasible Polygon & Solve the Intersection System\n- On the **horizontal $x_1$-axis**, the intercepts are $(4,0)$ and $(2,0)$. The tighter one is **$A = (2, 0)$**.\n- On the **vertical $x_2$-axis**, the intercepts are $(0,3)$ and $(0,7)$. The tighter one is **$C = (0, 3)$**.\n- Inside the first quadrant, lines $D_1$ and $D_2$ cross at **Corner $B$**. Let's solve the system:\n  $$\\begin{cases} 3x_1 + 4x_2 = 12 & \\text{(1)} \\\\ 7x_1 + 2x_2 = 14 & \\text{(2)} \\end{cases}$$\n  - Multiply Equation (2) by $2$ so the $x_2$ coefficients match ($4x_2$):\n    $$14x_1 + 4x_2 = 28 \\quad \\text{(2')}$$\n  - Subtract Equation (1) from Equation (2'):\n    $$(14x_1 + 4x_2) - (3x_1 + 4x_2) = 28 - 12 \\implies 11x_1 = 16 \\implies x_1 = \\frac{16}{11} \\approx 1.4545$$\n  - Substitute $x_1 = \\frac{16}{11}$ into Equation (2):\n    $$7\\left(\\frac{16}{11}\\right) + 2x_2 = 14 \\implies \\frac{112}{11} + 2x_2 = \\frac{154}{11} \\implies 2x_2 = \\frac{42}{11} \\implies x_2 = \\frac{21}{11} \\approx 1.9091$$\n  - So **Corner $B = \\left(\\frac{16}{11}, \\frac{21}{11}\\right)$**.\n\n---\n\n#### Step 3: Apply the Parallel Lines Method & Corner Table\n- **Plot a reference Iso-Profit Line $\\Delta_0$:** Pick $Z_0 = 12$, giving $4x_1 + 3x_2 = 12$, which passes through $(0, 4)$ and $(3, 0)$.\n- Sliding $\\Delta_0$ parallel outward away from $(0,0)$, the last point touched is **Corner $B$**. Let's verify in the Corner Table:\n\n| Vertex | Coordinates $(x_1, x_2)$ | Substitute into $Z = 4x_1 + 3x_2$ | Value of $Z$ |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- | :---: |\n| **$O$** | $(0, 0)$ | $4(0) + 3(0)$ | $0$ |\n| **$A$** | $(2, 0)$ | $4(2) + 3(0)$ | $8$ |\n| **$C$** | $(0, 3)$ | $4(0) + 3(3)$ | $9$ |\n| **$B$ 🏆** | **$\\left(\\frac{16}{11}, \\frac{21}{11}\\right)$** | **$4\\left(\\frac{16}{11}\\right) + 3\\left(\\frac{21}{11}\\right) = \\frac{64 + 63}{11}$** | **$\\frac{127}{11} \\approx 11.545$** |\n\n✅ **Optimal Solution:** $x_1^* = \\frac{16}{11},\\; x_2^* = \\frac{21}{11}$ with maximum objective **$Z^* = \\frac{127}{11} \\approx 11.55$**."
