        "title": "Example 2.3: Converting a Trickier Mixed-Constraint Problem to Standard Form",
        "badge": "Level 3 — Negative RHS, Surplus & Unrestricted Variable",
        "problem": "Convert the following Linear Program into **Standard Form** (ready for Simplex):\n$$\\min W = 2x_1 - 5x_2 + 3x_3$$\n$$\\text{subject to:} \\quad \\begin{cases} -x_1 + 2x_2 - x_3 \\le -8 & (1) \\\\ 3x_1 + x_2 + 4x_3 \\le 15 & (2) \\\\ 2x_1 - x_2 = 4 & (3) \\\\ x_1 \\ge 0,\\; x_2 \\ge 0,\\; x_3 \\in \\mathbb{R} \\text{ (unrestricted)} \\end{cases}$$",
        "solution": "Let's fix each issue one by one using our 3 Standard Form rules:\n\n1. **Fix the Objective Function ($\\min W \\to \\max Z$):**\n   Multiply $W$ by $-1$ and let $Z = -W$:\n   $$\\max Z = -2x_1 + 5x_2 - 3x_3$$\n\n2. **Fix the Unrestricted Variable $x_3 \\in \\mathbb{R}$:**\n   Substitute $x_3 = x_3^+ - x_3^-$ with $x_3^+ \\ge 0,\\; x_3^- \\ge 0$ everywhere!\n\n3. **Fix Constraint (1) (Negative Right-Hand Side $b_1 = -8 < 0$):**\n   - First multiply Constraint (1) by $-1$ and **flip $\\le$ to $\\ge$**:\n     $$x_1 - 2x_2 + x_3 \\ge 8$$\n   - Because it is now $\\ge 8$, **subtract a surplus variable $-e_1 \\ge 0$** and replace $x_3 = x_3^+ - x_3^-$:\n     $$x_1 - 2x_2 + x_3^+ - x_3^- - e_1 = 8$$\n\n4. **Fix Constraint (2) ($\\le 15$):**\n   - Since $15 \\ge 0$ and the sign is $\\le$, **add a slack variable $+e_2 \\ge 0$**:\n     $$3x_1 + x_2 + 4x_3^+ - 4x_3^- + e_2 = 15$$\n\n5. **Constraint (3) ($= 4$):**\n   - Already an equality with $b_3 = 4 \\ge 0$:\n     $$2x_1 - x_2 = 4$$\n\n✅ **Complete Standard Form:**\n$$\\max Z = -2x_1 + 5x_2 - 3x_3^+ + 3x_3^-$$\n$$\\text{subject to:} \\quad \\begin{cases}\nx_1 - 2x_2 + x_3^+ - x_3^- - e_1 = 8 \\\\\n3x_1 + x_2 + 4x_3^+ - 4x_3^- + e_2 = 15 \\\\\n2x_1 - x_2 = 4 \\\\\nx_1, x_2, x_3^+, x_3^-, e_1, e_2 \\ge 0\n\\end{cases}$$"
