        "title": "Example 3.1 (Clean Numbers Warm-Up): Complete 2-Pivot Simplex Tableau Walkthrough",
        "badge": "Level 1 — Every Row Operation Written Out",
        "problem": "Solve the following Linear Program using the **Simplex Tableau Method**, showing every single row operation and intermediate tableau:\n$$\\max Z = 5x_1 + 4x_2 \\quad \\text{subject to:} \\quad \\begin{cases} x_1 + x_2 \\le 20 \\\\ 2x_1 + x_2 \\le 35 \\\\ x_1, x_2 \\ge 0 \\end{cases}$$",
        "solution": "#### Step 0: Standard Form & Initial Tableau (Tableau 0)\nAdd slack variables $e_1, e_2 \\ge 0$:\n$$\\begin{cases} 1x_1 + 1x_2 + 1e_1 + 0e_2 = 20 \\\\ 2x_1 + 1x_2 + 0e_1 + 1e_2 = 35 \\end{cases}$$\n\n**Tableau 0 (Initial Corner: $x_1=0, x_2=0, e_1=20, e_2=35, Z=0$):**\n\n| $c_B$ | Basis | $x_1$ ($5$) | $x_2$ ($4$) | $e_1$ ($0$) | $e_2$ ($0$) | RHS ($b_i$) | Ratio ($b_i / a_{i1}$) |\n| :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: |\n| $0$ | $e_1$ | $1$ | $1$ | $1$ | $0$ | $20$ | $20 / 1 = 20$ |\n| $0$ | **$e_2$** $\\leftarrow$ | **$[2]$** | $1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $35$ | **$35 / 2 = 17.5$** (Min!) |\n| — | **$c_j - z_j$** | **$+5$** $\\uparrow$ | $+4$ | $0$ | $0$ | **$Z = 0$** | — |\n\n- **Entering Variable ($x_e$):** $\\max(5, 4) = 5 > 0 \\implies$ **$x_1$ enters** (Column 1).\n- **Leaving Variable ($x_s$):** $\\min(20,\\; 17.5) = 17.5 \\implies$ **$e_2$ leaves** (Row 2).\n- **Pivot Element:** $p = 2$ (at Row 2, Column $x_1$).\n\n---\n\n#### Pivot 1 Arithmetic (Moving from Tableau 0 $\\to$ Tableau 1)\n1. **Normalize Pivot Row 2 (divide Row 2 by $p = 2$):**\n   $$R_2^{\\text{new}} = \\frac{1}{2} R_2^{\\text{old}} = \\frac{1}{2}[2,\\; 1,\\; 0,\\; 1 \\mid 35] = \\left[1,\\; \\frac{1}{2},\\; 0,\\; \\frac{1}{2} \\;\\middle|\\; \\frac{35}{2}\\right]$$\n2. **Update Row 1 (eliminate the $1$ under $x_1$ in Row 1 using $R_1^{\\text{new}} = R_1^{\\text{old}} - 1 \\times R_2^{\\text{new}}$):**\n   $$\\begin{aligned}\n   R_1^{\\text{old}} &: \\quad \\left[1,\\quad 1,\\quad 1,\\quad 0 \\;\\middle|\\; 20\\right] \\\\\n   -1 \\times R_2^{\\text{new}} &: -\\left[1,\\quad \\frac{1}{2},\\quad 0,\\quad \\frac{1}{2} \\;\\middle|\\; \\frac{35}{2}\\right] \\\\\n   \\hline\n   R_1^{\\text{new}} &: \\quad \\left[0,\\quad \\frac{1}{2},\\quad 1,\\quad -\\frac{1}{2} \\;\\middle|\\; \\frac{5}{2}\\right]\n   \\end{aligned}$$\n3. **Update $c_j - z_j$ Row (using $(c_j - z_j)^{\\text{new}} = (c_j - z_j)^{\\text{old}} - 5 \\times R_2^{\\text{new}}$):**\n   $$\\begin{aligned}\n   (c_j - z_j)^{\\text{old}} &: \\quad \\left[5,\\quad 4,\\quad 0,\\quad 0\\right] \\\\\n   -5 \\times R_2^{\\text{new}} &: -\\left[5,\\quad \\frac{5}{2},\\quad 0,\\quad \\frac{5}{2}\\right] \\\\\n   \\hline\n   (c_j - z_j)^{\\text{new}} &: \\quad \\left[0,\\quad \\frac{3}{2},\\quad 0,\\quad -\\frac{5}{2}\\right], \\quad Z = 5 \\times \\frac{35}{2} = \\frac{175}{2} = 87.5\n   \\end{aligned}$$\n\n**Tableau 1 (After Iteration 1: $x_1 = 17.5, x_2 = 0, e_1 = 2.5, e_2 = 0, Z = 87.5$):**\n\n| $c_B$ | Basis | $x_1$ ($5$) | $x_2$ ($4$) | $e_1$ ($0$) | $e_2$ ($0$) | RHS ($b_i$) | Ratio ($b_i / a_{i2}$) |\n| :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: |\n| $0$ | **$e_1$** $\\leftarrow$ | $0$ | **$[1/2]$** | $1$ | $-1/2$ | $5/2$ | **$(5/2) / (1/2) = 5$** (Min!) |\n| $5$ | $x_1$ | $1$ | $1/2$ | $0$ | $1/2$ | $35/2$ | $(35/2) / (1/2) = 35$ |\n| — | **$c_j - z_j$** | $0$ | **$+3/2$** $\\uparrow$ | $0$ | $-5/2$ | **$Z = 175/2$** | — |\n\n- **Are we optimal?** No, because $x_2$ still has a positive reduced cost $+3/2 > 0$.\n- **Entering Variable ($x_e$):** **$x_2$ enters** (Column 2).\n- **Leaving Variable ($x_s$):** $\\min(5, 35) = 5 \\implies$ **$e_1$ leaves** (Row 1).\n- **Pivot Element:** $p = 1/2$ (at Row 1, Column $x_2$).\n\n---\n\n#### Pivot 2 Arithmetic (Moving from Tableau 1 $\\to$ Tableau 2)\n1. **Normalize Pivot Row 1 (divide Row 1 by $p = 1/2$, which means multiply by $2$):**\n   $$R_1^{\\text{new}} = 2 \\times R_1^{\\text{old}} = 2 \\times \\left[0,\\; \\frac{1}{2},\\; 1,\\; -\\frac{1}{2} \\;\\middle|\\; \\frac{5}{2}\\right] = \\left[0,\\; 1,\\; 2,\\; -1 \\;\\middle|\\; 5\\right]$$\n2. **Update Row 2 (eliminate the $1/2$ under $x_2$ in Row 2 using $R_2^{\\text{new}} = R_2^{\\text{old}} - \\frac{1}{2} R_1^{\\text{new}}$):**\n   $$\\begin{aligned}\n   R_2^{\\text{old}} &: \\quad \\left[1,\\quad \\frac{1}{2},\\quad 0,\\quad \\frac{1}{2} \\;\\middle|\\; \\frac{35}{2}\\right] \\\\\n   -\\frac{1}{2} \\times R_1^{\\text{new}} &: -\\left[0,\\quad \\frac{1}{2},\\quad 1,\\quad -\\frac{1}{2} \\;\\middle|\\; \\frac{5}{2}\\right] \\\\\n   \\hline\n   R_2^{\\text{new}} &: \\quad \\left[1,\\quad 0,\\quad -1,\\quad 1 \\;\\middle|\\; 15\\right]\n   \\end{aligned}$$\n3. **Update $c_j - z_j$ Row (using $(c_j - z_j)^{\\text{new}} = (c_j - z_j)^{\\text{old}} - \\frac{3}{2} R_1^{\\text{new}}$):**\n   $$\\begin{aligned}\n   (c_j - z_j)^{\\text{old}} &: \\quad \\left[0,\\quad \\frac{3}{2},\\quad 0,\\quad -\\frac{5}{2}\\right] \\\\\n   -\\frac{3}{2} \\times R_1^{\\text{new}} &: -\\left[0,\\quad \\frac{3}{2},\\quad 3,\\quad -\\frac{3}{2}\\right] \\\\\n   \\hline\n   (c_j - z_j)^{\\text{new}} &: \\quad \\left[0,\\quad 0,\\quad -3,\\quad -1\\right], \\quad Z = 4(5) + 5(15) = 95\n   \\end{aligned}$$\n\n**Tableau 2 (Final Optimal Tableau):**\n\n| $c_B$ | Basis | $x_1$ ($5$) | $x_2$ ($4$) | $e_1$ ($0$) | $e_2$ ($0$) | RHS ($b_i$) |\n| :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: |\n| $4$ | **$x_2$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $-1$ | **$5$** |\n| $5$ | **$x_1$** | $1$ | $0$ | $-1$ | $1$ | **$15$** |\n| — | **$c_j - z_j$** | $0$ | $0$ | **$-3$** | **$-1$** | **$Z^* = 95$** |\n\n✅ **Optimality Reached:** Every entry in $c_j - z_j$ is $\\le 0$ ($0, 0, -3, -1$).\nReading the **Basis** and **RHS** columns: **$x_1^* = 15,\\; x_2^* = 5$**, non-basic $e_1^* = e_2^* = 0$, and **$Z^* = 95$**!"
