    "theory": "### Quick Reference Summary — Chapter 5 Duality & Complementary Slackness\n- **Standard Primal-Dual Pair:**\n  $$(P) \\; \\max Z = c^T x \\;\\text{s.t.}\\; Ax \\le b,\\; x \\ge 0 \\quad \\Longleftrightarrow \\quad (D) \\; \\min W = b^T y \\;\\text{s.t.}\\; A^T y \\ge c,\\; y \\ge 0$$\n- **The 4-Step Complementary Slackness Algorithm (Given $x^*$, Find $y^*$):**\n  1. **Plug $x^*$ into each Primal Constraint $i$:**\n     - If $\\sum_j a_{ij} x_j^* < b_i$ (Slack $e_i^* > 0$) $\\implies$ immediately write **$y_i^* = 0$**!\n  2. **Look at which Primal Variables $x_j^*$ are strictly positive ($x_j^* > 0$):**\n     - For every $j$ with $x_j^* > 0$, turn **Dual Constraint $j$** from $\\ge c_j$ into an **exact equation $= c_j$**!\n  3. **Solve the small linear system** of equations for the remaining unknown $y_i^*$ values.\n  4. **Verify $Z^* = W^*$:** Compute $W^* = \\sum b_i y_i^*$ and confirm it equals $Z^* = \\sum c_j x_j^*$.",
