        "badge": "Level 1 — Writing the Dual (Standard & Mixed Signs)",
        "problem": "**Part A (Standard 3-Variable LP):** Write the Dual of:\n$$\\max Z = 5x_1 + 4x_2 + 3x_3 \\quad \\text{s.t.} \\quad \\begin{cases} 2x_1 + 3x_2 + x_3 \\le 5 & (y_1) \\\\ 4x_1 + x_2 + 2x_3 \\le 11 & (y_2) \\\\ 3x_1 + 4x_2 + 2x_3 \\le 8 & (y_3) \\\\ x_1, x_2, x_3 \\ge 0 \\end{cases}$$\n**Part B (Mixed Constraints & Free Variable):** Write the Dual of:\n$$\\max Z = 4x_1 + 3x_2 \\quad \\text{s.t.} \\quad \\begin{cases} 2x_1 + x_2 \\le 10 & (y_1) \\\\ x_1 - x_2 \\ge 2 & (y_2) \\\\ 3x_1 + 2x_2 = 12 & (y_3) \\\\ x_1 \\ge 0,\\; x_2 \\in \\mathbb{R} \\text{ (free)} \\end{cases}$$",
        "solution": "#### Solution to Part A (Standard Symmetric Dual)\n1. **Dual Variables:** 3 primal constraints $\\implies$ 3 dual variables **$y_1, y_2, y_3$**.\n2. **Objective ($\\max Z \\to \\min W$):** Use the Primal RHS $(5, 11, 8)$:\n   $$\\min W = 5y_1 + 11y_2 + 8y_3$$\n3. **Dual Constraints (Transpose columns of $x_1, x_2, x_3$ into rows):**\n   - **Column $x_1$ ($2, 4, 3$ with $c_1 = 5$ and $x_1 \\ge 0$):**\n     $$2y_1 + 4y_2 + 3y_3 \\ge 5$$\n   - **Column $x_2$ ($3, 1, 4$ with $c_2 = 4$ and $x_2 \\ge 0$):**\n     $$3y_1 + 1y_2 + 4y_3 \\ge 4$$\n   - **Column $x_3$ ($1, 2, 2$ with $c_3 = 3$ and $x_3 \\ge 0$):**\n     $$1y_1 + 2y_2 + 2y_3 \\ge 3$$\n4. **Signs of $y_i$:** Since all 3 primal constraints are $\\le$, all 3 dual variables are non-negative:\n   $$y_1 \\ge 0, \\quad y_2 \\ge 0, \\quad y_3 \\ge 0$$\n\n---\n\n#### Solution to Part B (Mixed Constraints & Unrestricted Variable)\n1. **Objective ($\\max Z \\to \\min W$):** Use the Primal RHS $(10, 2, 12)$:\n   $$\\min W = 10y_1 + 2y_2 + 12y_3$$\n2. **Dual Constraints (from columns $x_1$ and $x_2$):**\n   - **Column $x_1$ ($2, 1, 3$ with $c_1 = 4$):** Since **$x_1 \\ge 0$** (standard), Dual Constraint 1 is **$\\ge 4$**:\n     $$2y_1 + y_2 + 3y_3 \\ge 4$$\n   - **Column $x_2$ ($1, -1, 2$ with $c_2 = 3$):** Since **$x_2 \\in \\mathbb{R}$ (free/unrestricted)**, Dual Constraint 2 is an **exact equality ($= 3$)**!\n     $$1y_1 - 1y_2 + 2y_3 = 3$$\n3. **Signs of $y_1, y_2, y_3$ (from Primal Constraint signs):**\n   - Primal Row 1 is $\\le 10$ (standard for Max) $\\implies$ **$y_1 \\ge 0$**\n   - Primal Row 2 is $\\ge 2$ (reversed for Max) $\\implies$ **$y_2 \\le 0$**\n   - Primal Row 3 is $= 12$ (equality) $\\implies$ **$y_3 \\in \\mathbb{R}$ (unrestricted in sign)**!"
