        "question": "In Example 3.3 (the 3-variable K. ISKAFI problem $\\max Z = 20x_1 + 16x_2 + 12x_3$), at the final optimal tableau (Tableau 4), **$x_1$ was Non-Basic ($x_1^* = 0$)** and its bottom-row entry was **$c_1 - z_1 = -4$**.\nHow much must the selling price $c_1$ (currently $20$) increase before it becomes profitable to produce $x_1$? What is the stability interval of $c_1$?",
        "solution": "Because $x_1$ is **Non-Basic ($x_1^* = 0$)**, changing $c_1 \\to 20 + \\delta$ only changes $x_1$'s own reduced cost:\n$$(c_1 - z_1)_{\\text{new}} = -4 + \\delta \\le 0 \\implies \\delta \\le 4$$\nAdding $c_1 = 20$ gives:\n$$\\boxed{c_1' \\in (-\\infty,\\; 24]}$$\n✅ **Interpretation:** You must raise the selling price of $x_1$ above **$24$** (an increase of more than $+4$) before producing $x_1$ becomes worthwhile!"
