    "workedExample": {
      "title": "Example 6.1 (Warm-Up): Complete Sensitivity Analysis on a 2×2 Tableau",
      "badge": "Level 1 — Step-by-Step c1 Range, b1 Range & Shadow Price",
      "problem": "Consider the Linear Program:\n$$\\max Z = 5x_1 + 4x_2 \\quad \\text{subject to:} \\quad \\begin{cases} 6x_1 + 4x_2 \\le 24 & (e_1) \\\\ x_1 + 2x_2 \\le 6 & (e_2) \\\\ x_1, x_2 \\ge 0 \\end{cases}$$\n1. Solve the LP by Simplex Tableaux to reach the optimal tableau.\n2. Find the **optimality range of $c_1$** ($c_1' = 5 + \\delta$) so the optimal basis remains unchanged.\n3. Find the **feasibility range of $b_1$** ($b_1' = 24 + \\Delta$) and the **Shadow Price $y_1^*$** of Resource 1. What is the new optimal profit if $b_1$ increases from $24$ to $30$?",
      "solution": "#### Part 1: Solving by Simplex Tableaux from Tableau 0 to Optimal Tableau 2\n**Tableau 0 (Initial Basis $e_1 = 24, e_2 = 6, Z = 0$):**\n\n| $c_B$ | Basis | $x_1$ ($5$) | $x_2$ ($4$) | $e_1$ ($0$) | $e_2$ ($0$) | RHS ($b_i$) | Ratio ($b_i / a_{i1}$) |\n| :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: |\n| $0$ | **$e_1$** $\\leftarrow$ | **$[6]$** | $4$ | $1$ | $0$ | $24$ | **$24 / 6 = 4$** (Min!) |\n| $0$ | $e_2$ | $1$ | $2$ | $0$ | $1$ | $6$ | $6 / 1 = 6$ |\n| — | **$c_j - z_j$** | **$+5$** $\\uparrow$ | $+4$ | $0$ | $0$ | **$Z = 0$** | — |\n\n- **Pivot 1:** $x_1$ enters ($+5$), $e_1$ leaves ($4$). Pivot $p = 6$.\n  - $R_1' = \\frac{1}{6} R_1 = [1,\\; 2/3,\\; 1/6,\\; 0 \\mid 4]$\n  - $R_2' = R_2 - 1 R_1' = [0,\\; 4/3,\\; -1/6,\\; 1 \\mid 2]$\n  - $(c_j - z_j)' = [5, 4, 0, 0] - 5[1, 2/3, 1/6, 0] = [0,\\; +2/3,\\; -5/6,\\; 0]$\n\n**Tableau 1 (Basis: $x_1 = 4, e_2 = 2, Z = 20$):**\n\n| $c_B$ | Basis | $x_1$ ($5$) | $x_2$ ($4$) | $e_1$ ($0$) | $e_2$ ($0$) | RHS ($b_i$) | Ratio ($b_i / a_{i2}$) |\n| :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: |\n| $5$ | $x_1$ | $1$ | $2/3$ | $1/6$ | $0$ | $4$ | $4 / (2/3) = 6$ |\n| $0$ | **$e_2$** $\\leftarrow$ | $0$ | **$[4/3]$** | $-1/6$ | $1$ | $2$ | **$2 / (4/3) = 1.5$** (Min!) |\n| — | **$c_j - z_j$** | $0$ | **$+2/3$** $\\uparrow$ | $-5/6$ | $0$ | **$Z = 20$** | — |\n\n- **Pivot 2:** $x_2$ enters ($+2/3$), $e_2$ leaves ($1.5$). Pivot $p = 4/3$.\n  - $R_2' = \\frac{3}{4} R_2 = [0,\\; 1,\\; -1/8,\\; 3/4 \\mid 3/2]$\n  - $R_1' = R_1 - \\frac{2}{3} R_2' = [1,\\; 0,\\; 1/4,\\; -1/2 \\mid 3]$\n  - $(c_j - z_j)' = [0, 2/3, -5/6, 0] - \\frac{2}{3}[0, 1, -1/8, 3/4] = [0,\\; 0,\\; -3/4,\\; -1/2]$\n\n**Tableau 2 (Final Optimal Tableau: $x_1^* = 3, x_2^* = 1.5, Z^* = 21$):**\n\n| $c_B$ | Basis | $x_1$ ($5$) | $x_2$ ($4$) | $e_1$ ($0$) | $e_2$ ($0$) | RHS ($b_i$) |\n| :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: |\n| $5$ | **$x_1$** | $1$ | $0$ | **$1/4$** | **$-1/2$** | **$3$** |\n| $4$ | **$x_2$** | $0$ | $1$ | **$-1/8$** | **$3/4$** | **$3/2$ ($1.5$)** |\n| — | **$c_j - z_j$** | $0$ | $0$ | **$-3/4$** | **$-1/2$** | **$Z^* = 21$** |\n\n---\n\n#### Part 2: Sensitivity of $c_1$ ($c_1' = 5 + \\delta$) Using the Optimal Tableau\nSince **$x_1$ is Basic in Row 1**, we look across **Row 1** at the **Non-Basic columns ($e_1$ and $e_2$)**:\n- In Row 1, under $e_1$: entry is **$a_{1,e_1} = +1/4$**, and old $(c_{e_1} - z_{e_1}) = -3/4$.\n- In Row 1, under $e_2$: entry is **$a_{1,e_2} = -1/2$**, and old $(c_{e_2} - z_{e_2}) = -1/2$.\n\nApply the formula $(c_j - z_j)_{\\text{new}} = (c_j - z_j)_{\\text{old}} - \\delta \\cdot a_{1j} \\le 0$:\n1. **Column $e_1$:**\n   $$-\\frac{3}{4} - \\delta\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right) \\le 0 \\implies -\\frac{1}{4}\\delta \\le \\frac{3}{4} \\implies \\mathbf{\\delta \\ge -3}$$\n2. **Column $e_2$:**\n   $$-\\frac{1}{2} - \\delta\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\le 0 \\implies +\\frac{1}{2}\\delta \\le \\frac{1}{2} \\implies \\mathbf{\\delta \\le +1}$$\n\nCombine both inequalities:\n$$-3 \\le \\delta \\le 1 \\xrightarrow{+5} 5 - 3 \\le 5 + \\delta \\le 5 + 1 \\implies \\boxed{c_1' \\in [2,\\; 6]}$$\n\n---\n\n#### Part 3: Sensitivity of $b_1$ ($b_1' = 24 + \\Delta$) & Shadow Price $y_1^*$\nLook down the **Slack Column $e_1$** ($[1/4,\\; -1/8]^T$) and the **RHS Column** ($[3,\\; 3/2]^T$) in Tableau 2:\n$$\\text{RHS}_{\\text{new}} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 3/2 \\end{pmatrix} + \\Delta \\begin{pmatrix} 1/4 \\\\ -1/8 \\end{pmatrix} \\ge \\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}$$\n1. **Row 1 ($x_1 \\ge 0$):**\n   $$3 + \\frac{1}{4}\\Delta \\ge 0 \\implies \\frac{1}{4}\\Delta \\ge -3 \\implies \\mathbf{\\Delta \\ge -12}$$\n2. **Row 2 ($x_2 \\ge 0$):**\n   $$\\frac{3}{2} - \\frac{1}{8}\\Delta \\ge 0 \\implies \\frac{1}{8}\\Delta \\le \\frac{3}{2} \\implies \\mathbf{\\Delta \\le +12}$$\n\nCombine both inequalities:\n$$-12 \\le \\Delta \\le 12 \\xrightarrow{+24} 24 - 12 \\le 24 + \\Delta \\le 24 + 12 \\implies \\boxed{b_1' \\in [12,\\; 36]}$$\n- **Shadow Price of Resource 1 ($y_1^*$):** Read under $e_1$ in the bottom row:\n  $$y_1^* = -(c_{e_1} - z_{e_1})^* = -\\left(-\\frac{3}{4}\\right) = \\boxed{\\frac{3}{4} = 0.75}$$\n- **If $b_1$ increases from $24$ to $30$ ($\\Delta = +6 \\in [-12, 12]$):**\n  The basis stays valid, and the new optimal profit is:\n  $$Z_{\\text{new}}^* = Z_{\\text{old}}^* + \\Delta \\cdot y_1^* = 21 + 6(0.75) = 21 + 4.5 = \\boxed{25.5!}$$"
    }
