        "title": "Lesson 7.1 — The 4 Words of Branch-and-Bound: Relax, Bound, Branch, Prune!",
        "content": "Every Branch-and-Bound (B&B) problem (for Maximization $\\max Z$) follows the exact same **4-word cycle**:\n\n1. **RELAX (Relâcher):**\n   Drop the integer restriction ($x_j \\in \\mathbb{Z}_+ \\to x_j \\ge 0$, or $x_j \\in \\{0,1\\} \\to 0 \\le x_j \\le 1$) and solve the continuous LP at **Node 0 (Root Node)**.\n2. **BOUND (Évaluer):**\n   The continuous solution at a node gives an **Upper Bound $UB = Z_{LP}$** (or you can round it down to $\\lfloor Z_{LP} \\rfloor$ if all objective coefficients $c_j$ are integers!). No integer descendant inside that branch can **ever** beat its parent's $UB$!\n   Meanwhile, the best **100% integer solution** you have discovered so far anywhere in the tree is stored as your **Champion Lower Bound ($LB = Z_{\\text{best int}}$)**.\n3. **BRANCH (Séparer):**\n   Pick a variable $x_k$ whose value at the current node is **fractional** (e.g., $x_k^* = 2.75$, or $x_3 = 2/3$ in 0/1 Knapsack) and create **2 child nodes**:\n   - **For General Integers ($x_k \\in \\mathbb{Z}_+$):** Left branch **$x_k \\le \\lfloor x_k^* \\rfloor$** and Right branch **$x_k \\ge \\lceil x_k^* \\rceil$**.\n   - **For Binary 0/1 Knapsack ($x_k \\in \\{0, 1\\}$):** Left branch **$x_k = 1$ (take item $k$)** and Right branch **$x_k = 0$ (skip item $k$)**.\n4. **PRUNE / FATHOM (Élaguer / Stériliser — When Do We STOP Branching from a Node?):**\n   You **stop (prune)** a node immediately in **3 situations**:\n   - **Reason A (Integer Achieved ✅):** All variables $x_j$ at the node are integers! If its $Z > LB$, crown it as the **new Champion $LB$**!\n   - **Reason B (Infeasible ❌):** The fixed variables already exceed the budget/constraints ($S = \\emptyset$).\n   - **Reason C (Bound Dominated $\\le LB$ ✂️):** The node's Upper Bound $UB \\le LB$ (it cannot possibly beat the integer champion we already have in our pocket!)."
